Package: robscale
Type: Package
Title: Robust Estimation in Small Samples via SIMD-Accelerated Iteration
Version: 0.1.1
Authors@R: c(person(given = "Dennis Alexis Valin", family = "Dittrich",
    role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"), email = "davd@economicscience.net",
    comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-4438-8276")))
Description: Provides a high-performance C++ implementation of the robust
    location and scale M-estimators described in Rousseeuw & Verboven (2002)
    <doi:10.1016/S0167-9473(02)00078-6>. This package optimizes the logistic
    M-estimators for measurements with very small sample sizes ($n \leq 8$) using
    platform-specific SIMD vectorization (Apple Accelerate and SLEEF),
    Newton--Raphson iteration, and sorting networks. Across 5,400 cross-checks,
    'robscale' maintains numerical equivalence to the 'revss' package while
    reducing execution time by a factor of 11--39 in the target regime.
